# Build-context prune for the deploy pack (WAVE 5). Keep the context small and
# NEVER ship host-installed deps, compiled output, runtime state, or secrets.
.git
.gitignore
**/node_modules
**/dist
web/dist
harness/dist
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.serena
**/*.log

# Runtime artifacts (regenerated inside the containers / on named volumes)
server/jobs.db
server/jobs.db-shm
server/jobs.db-wal
server/broker_ledger.jsonl
server/broker_tenants.json
# _save_tenants mkstemps its replacement as `.broker_tenants.json.<rand>.tmp`
# beside the snapshot (server/broker.py); the leading dot keeps it outside a
# `broker_tenants.json*` widening.
server/.broker_tenants.json.*
# Broker/jobs restart-survival sidecars and the site-demo solve cache. All three
# Dockerfiles that `COPY server/` (app, broker, canonical-worker) would bake a
# dev's local copies into the image, and none is read from /app/server at
# runtime: BROKER_LEDGER and JOBS_DB point these at /data/state
# (docker-compose.yml), which is where broker.py and jobs.py derive them from.
# The trailing * / dotted glob cover the .tmp siblings each writer replaces
# through, one of which embeds a pid and a thread id.
server/active_workitems.jsonl*
server/pending_reaps.jsonl*
server/site_demo_cache.json
server/.site_demo_cache.json.*
# Materialized tenant catalog worktrees plus the `.materialize.lock` one level
# in (server/customization_service.py). Checked out at runtime from the tenant
# bare repo, and the deployed containers set LEAF_EFFECTIVE_TENANTS_DIR
# explicitly (deploy/required-config.{app,broker}.json), so nothing reads this
# path inside an image.
server/customization-worktrees/
server/agent_tenants.json*
server/authored_tools.json
server/drawings/
# Session + customization SQLite DBs, with their WAL/SHM sidecars. Written at
# runtime, redirected to the leaf-state volume in the containers (SESSIONS_DB,
# docker-compose.yml), and never git-tracked, so a clean CI checkout has none
# of them. Without these lines a dev who ran the server locally bakes their own
# sessions into both images.
server/sessions.db
server/sessions.db-shm
server/sessions.db-wal
server/customization.db
server/customization.db-shm
server/customization.db-wal
# Guest drawing store: raw user-supplied DWG/DXF written at runtime under
# guest_store_dir() (server/write_loop.py, LEAF_GUEST_STORE_DIR). Same
# customer-data class as data/uploads/ below.
server/guest_drawings/
# Guest uploads: raw user-supplied DWG/DXF written at runtime
# (server/routers/uploads.py). Already git-ignored; keep them out of images too.
data/uploads/
# Agent gate-chain state, written at runtime. Both Dockerfiles do
# `COPY data/ /app/data/`, but the gate-state files are redirected to
# /data/state on the leaf-state volume (docker-compose.yml), and no current
# code provisions or reads data/workspaces/, so nothing in either image reads
# any of them. A dev who ran the server locally would otherwise bake stale gate
# decisions and session grants into both images. The trailing * covers the
# sibling .tmp and .lock files (server/agent_gate.py).
data/agent_audit.jsonl
data/agent_ledger.jsonl
data/agent.disabled
data/agent_approvals/
data/agent_session_grants.json*
data/agent_rate_state.json*
data/workspaces/

# Compiled output from the LeafWriteTools .NET appbundle
# (engine/appbundle-write/BUILD.md). Both Dockerfiles COPY engine/ wholesale
# (deploy/Dockerfile.app, deploy/Dockerfile.broker), so a dev who built the
# bundle and then ran `docker compose build` (RUN.md, deploy/README.md) bakes
# their own build tree into both images. Already git-ignored, so a clean CI
# checkout has none of them. Per-directory on purpose: a bare `engine/` would
# drop the tracked appbundle sources the images need.
engine/appbundle-write/bin/
engine/appbundle-write/obj/
engine/appbundle-write/build/

# Local env / secrets — must never enter an image layer
**/.env.local
# Vite's other local-env files. The line above is one exact name; Vite also
# loads `.env.<mode>.local` (`.env.production.local` and friends), which is why
# web/.gitignore:4 lists a bare `*.local` beside `.env.local`. Docker reads no
# nested ignore file, so that rule covers nothing here, and `COPY web/ /web/`
# (deploy/Dockerfile.web:23) would put such a file into the build-stage layer.
# Repo-wide like the neighboring patterns; no tracked file matches it.
**/*.local
.env
.secrets/
**/.grant/
# demo tenant checkouts the harness tests create
harness/.tmp/
harness/tenant-checkouts/

# The deploy pack itself is referenced by dockerfile path, not copied wholesale
# (kept out of the python/node source COPYs implicitly).
